WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.259
Quick question.

2
00:00:01.539 --> 00:00:04.374
Why would anyone pay more for a watch than for a used car?

3
00:00:04.654 --> 00:00:08.020
It tells the same time as your phone. And your phone has games.

4
00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:10.629
Welcome to prestige pricing.

5
00:00:10.909 --> 00:00:13.601
That's when a company sets a high price on purpose,

6
00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:17.031
because buyers see the high price as part of what they're buying.

7
00:00:17.981 --> 00:00:19.976
Rolex builds that feeling three ways.

8
00:00:20.256 --> 00:00:23.577
First, scarcity. Popular models can be hard to find,

9
00:00:23.577 --> 00:00:26.323
and some buyers wait months, or even years.

10
00:00:26.603 --> 00:00:30.912
Second, status. Wearing one tells everyone at the barbecue that you've made it.

11
00:00:31.192 --> 00:00:35.872
Third, quality. Fine craftsmanship gives buyers a reason to believe the price.

12
00:00:36.822 --> 00:00:37.778
Here's the twist.

13
00:00:38.058 --> 00:00:41.178
For most products, a lower price brings in more buyers.

14
00:00:41.458 --> 00:00:46.048
For prestige products, cut the price too far, and demand can actually drop.

15
00:00:46.328 --> 00:00:49.241
If everyone can afford it, it isn't special anymore.

16
00:00:50.191 --> 00:00:53.651
So the price isn't just covering costs. It's part of the brand.

17
00:00:53.931 --> 00:00:58.225
Your turn. Name another product people buy partly because it's expensive.
